{"uid":"a0dcd07d7c5cb1b7","name":"test_task_table_shows_summed_time_and_cost_across_two_iterations","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub#test_task_table_shows_summed_time_and_cost_across_two_iterations","historyId":"0855f9fc72e2d12994dc9ef7a9cd8cf4","time":{"start":1792070790720,"stop":1792070794450,"duration":3730},"description":"Task 036 (G.4), inverted for task 001/PRD I.1 (#207/#29): the hub\n    tasks table's time/cost columns are AGGREGATED per task, not the last\n    iteration's own figures -- a task that took two attempts WITHIN THE\n    RUN'S CURRENT APPROACH (a validation-failed re-entry dispatching a\n    second iteration against the SAME task id) must show the SUM across\n    both -- but that sum must never pick up an EARLIER approach's own dead\n    attempt at the same-numbered task id, exactly the cross-approach\n    summing bug #207 reported (\"$52.50 reported where $8.31 belonged\").\n\n    Three iterations, all `assignedTaskId: \"030\"`, spanning an approach\n    boundary: iteration 1 is a STALE approach 1 attempt (a big, easily\n    distinguished spend); iterations 2 and 3 are the run's CURRENT approach\n    2's own two attempts at the same-numbered task -- a validation-failed\n    first attempt and the re-claim that finished it -- each with its own\n    duration and its own fully-priced `usage`, built off the same\n    `_base_meta` fixture helper task 034's test above uses. The run's own\n    `status.json` records `approach: 2` (`_write_dead_run`'s override\n    below), so the hub must show ONLY approach 2's own figures for task\n    \"030\" -- the sum of iterations 2 and 3 -- never approach 1's iteration 1\n    folded in too. `engine.state.task_totals` sums `durationS` and rolls the\n    matching-approach `usage` dicts together (`_accumulate_task_usage`, the\n    same algorithm `LoopSupervisor._merge_usage` uses for status.json's own\n    buckets), so the expected total is computed here from the SAME two\n    (approach-2-only) numbers the fixture writes, never a hand-typed literal\n    that could drift from the fixture -- and is asserted to differ from what\n    a flat, approach-blind sum of all three iterations would have produced.\n\n    Against the pre-fix `task_totals` (bd94c695, before task 001/32044015\n    approach-namespaced the keys), this node fails: a flat `taskId`-only key\n    folds iteration 1's stale approach-1 spend into approach 2's task \"030\"\n    row, so `expected_time`/`expected_cost` below do not match what the row\n    actually renders (see the commit message for the captured failure).\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 036 (G.4), inverted for task 001/PRD I.1 (#207/#29): the hub<br />\ntasks table's time/cost columns are AGGREGATED per task, not the last<br />\niteration's own figures -- a task that took two attempts WITHIN THE<br />\nRUN'S CURRENT APPROACH (a validation-failed re-entry dispatching a<br />\nsecond iteration against the SAME task id) must show the SUM across<br />\nboth -- but that sum must never pick up an EARLIER approach's own dead<br />\nattempt at the same-numbered task id, exactly the cross-approach<br />\nsumming bug #207 reported (&quot;$52.50 reported where $8.31 belonged&quot;).</p>\n<pre><code>Three iterations, all `assignedTaskId: &quot;030&quot;`, spanning an approach\nboundary: iteration 1 is a STALE approach 1 attempt (a big, easily\ndistinguished spend); iterations 2 and 3 are the run's CURRENT approach\n2's own two attempts at the same-numbered task -- a validation-failed\nfirst attempt and the re-claim that finished it -- each with its own\nduration and its own fully-priced `usage`, built off the same\n`_base_meta` fixture helper task 034's test above uses. The run's own\n`status.json` records `approach: 2` (`_write_dead_run`'s override\nbelow), so the hub must show ONLY approach 2's own figures for task\n&quot;030&quot; -- the sum of iterations 2 and 3 -- never approach 1's iteration 1\nfolded in too. `engine.state.task_totals` sums `durationS` and rolls the\nmatching-approach `usage` dicts together (`_accumulate_task_usage`, the\nsame algorithm `LoopSupervisor._merge_usage` uses for status.json's own\nbuckets), so the expected total is computed here from the SAME two\n(approach-2-only) numbers the fixture writes, never a hand-typed literal\nthat could drift from the fixture -- and is asserted to differ from what\na flat, approach-blind sum of all three iterations would have produced.\n\nAgainst the pre-fix `task_totals` (bd94c695, before task 001/32044015\napproach-namespaced the keys), this node fails: a flat `taskId`-only key\nfolds iteration 1's stale approach-1 spend into approach 2's task &quot;030&quot;\nrow, so `expected_time`/`expected_cost` below do not match what the row\nactually renders (see the commit message for the captured failure).\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1792070371631,"stop":1792070371632,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1792070371632,"stop":1792070371632,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1792070790716,"stop":1792070790716,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1792070790717,"stop":1792070790718,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"ha